a/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kiranchavala","id":1401014,"login":"kiranchavala","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDEwMTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1401014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kiranchavala","id":1401014,"login":"kiranchavala","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDEwMTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiranchavala"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"\u003c!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\u003e\r\n * Documentation Report\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n\u003c!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nBuild instructions\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.16\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\nCentOS 7\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\u003e\r\nI tried to follow the steps in INSTALL.md to build CloudStack on CentOS 7.  The instructions aren't working.  They seem to be missing some steps, and I wonder if some of the dependency version numbers are outdated (e.g. Maven 3.6.3).\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\u003c!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\u003e\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nI had to add a MySQL repository before yum could install MySQL.  I didn't know which version to use, so I picked 7.5 because it's used in the quick installation guide.\r\n\r\n```\r\nwget http://repo.mysql.com/mysql-community-release-el7-5.noarch.rpm\r\nrpm -ivh mysql-community-release-el7-5.noarch.rpm\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn the `Install tools and dependencies` section, I needed to add bzip2 and python3 to the yum command.\r\n\r\nThe Maven download URL doesn't work.  You could change the domain name from www.us.apache.org to archive.apache.org.  That would work, but you'd still get an old version.  I found it was much easier to just use sdkman.io to install the latest version.\r\n\r\nThose changes were enough for the build to succeed.  But I couldn't create the DB schema.  I'm wondering if that part of the process needs an older version of MySQL.\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":4,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6726/comments","created_at":"2022-09-09T20:07:57Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6726/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/6726","id":1368274307,"labels":[{"color":"8236aa","default":false,"description":"","id":2479281588,"name":"component:documentation","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNDc5MjgxNTg4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:documentation"},{"color":"E43179","default":false,"description":"","id":6890295339,"name":"status:stale","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABmrGQKw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:stale"},{"color":"ededed","default":false,"id":9849008471,"name":"no-issue-activity","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6726/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":1302,"created_at":"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19","id":6265435,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels","node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==","number":19,"open_issues":185,"state":"open","title":"unplanned","updated_at":"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M5RjjWD","number":6726,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6726/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"INSTALL.md is incomplete and/or outdated","updated_at":"2026-08-17T02:00:25Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6726","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4752942?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mrog","id":4752942,"login":"mrog","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTI5NDI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrog"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"\u003c!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n * Enhancement Request\r\n \r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n~~~\r\nStorage\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n~~~\r\nAny\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\nUnmapping volumes from a hypervisor host upon VM stop or migration is done on a best-effort basis. The VM is already stopped, or already migrated, we try to unmap, but if something goes wrong there is really no recourse or retry and a warning is logged.  This leaves a potential of leaking maps to hosts over time.\r\n\r\nIn code review I've also found edge cases where a VM is moved to \"Stopped\" state without necessarily cleaning up network or volume resources, these can also lead to leaked maps over time. Examples are force removing a hypervisor host with running VMs on it, and possibly any other code that just calls `vm.setState(State.Stopped)`.\r\n\r\nMy request is that we be more thorough during VM start in ensuring that our target host and *only* our target host has access to the volume.  Or at least call the storage plugin involved to let it decide how to do this. It should be as simple as calling the storage service to \"revoke all\" just before we grant access, or allowing for an exclusive grant in the storage API.\r\n\r\nFor example, with the PowerFlex/ScaleIO storage client there is an `unmapVolumeFromAllSdcs` that could be called just prior to granting access to volumes during VM start. \r\n\r\nWe may need to add a `revokeAllAccess()` method to the `PrimaryDataStoreDriver`, or add a flag to the existing `revokeAccess` to indicate that the storage driver should revoke all.  \r\n\r\nOr alternatively (I think I like this better), the `grantAccess()` call might gain a flag `boolean exclusive` so the storage driver can be instructed to ensure that only one mapping exists - the one requested.  This would be cleaner.\r\n\r\nCrucially - we need to avoid exclusive access during the live migration workflows. It seems safe to ensure exclusive access during VM start, however.\r\n","comments":3,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6746/comments","created_at":"2022-09-16T15:38:14Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6746/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/6746","id":1376117413,"labels":[{"color":"84b6eb","default":false,"description":"","id":37843366,"name":"type:enhancement","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:enhancement"},{"color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"","id":4006883948,"name":"component:storage","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M7u1DJs","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:storage"},{"color":"E43179","default":false,"description":"","id":6890295339,"name":"status:stale","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABmrGQKw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:stale"},{"color":"ededed","default":false,"id":9849008471,"name":"no-issue-activity","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6746/labels{/name}","locked":false,"mile